id: illusion
name: Illusion
uaType: magical
prerequisite: Magic Score of 4+, 2+ Use Magic Skill Ranks, 2+ Bluff Skill Ranks
tpCost: 14
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerBaseTier: 4
# Its Square and who is inside the Sphere asked, with which Skill you roll (use-maneuver.mjs askIllusion); a Clash (Use
# Magic/Bluff vs Use Magic/Intuition/Clairvoyance) each, tallied on its card (chat.mjs postIllusion). Won against any:
# the 1d4 rolled there - or chosen by the ARC, or for a Karma Point - and that Combat Condition on every one who lost,
# until the end of your next turn.
illusion: true
illusionMagnitude: standard
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Sphere within 8 Squares: a Clash (Use Magic/Bluff vs Use Magic/Intuition/Clairvoyance) against every Opponent inside -
  won, 1d4 picks Blinded, Shaken, Impediment or Compelled for all who lost, until the end of your next turn. Passive: Bluff
  Skill Checks 1 higher.
text: >
  Illusion: You are capable of creating a combat illusion, deceiving your enemies.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: Magic Score of 4+, 2+ Use Magic Skill Ranks, 2+ Bluff Skill Ranks
  –TP Cost: 14
  –KP Cost: 4(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: Increase your Bluff Skill Checks by 1.
  –Effect: Target a Square within 8 Squares of you. Create a Sphere AoE centered on that Square. Make a Clash (Use
  Magic/Bluff vs Use Magic/Intuition/Clairvoyance) against all Opponents within that AoE. If you win, roll a 1d4.
  Depending on the result, apply one of the following Combat Conditions to all losing Opponents until the end of your
  next turn:

  * 1) Blinded,

  * 2) Shaken,

  * 3) Impediment,

  * 4) Compelled (the target must be another Character within the initial AoE created by this Unique Ability).

  Rather than roll, your ARC may choose an effect that seems fitting depending on your description for the Illusion you
  created through this Unique Ability. They may allow you to spend a Karma Point to choose.

---

# "Increase your Bluff Skill Checks by 1" - flat.
[passive]
skill.bluff.bonus += 1;
